{"questions":[{"question_id":"BClBtSUGp0NJL2jm","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2005","year":2005,"examDate":2005,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"coordination-compounds","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","topic":"warners-theory-and-valence-bond-theory","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"which-one-of-the-following-cyano-complexes-would-exhibit-the-2005-marks-4-bclbtsugp0njl2jm.htm","content":"Which one of the following cyano complexes would exhibit the lowest value of\nparamagnetic behaviour? <br>\n(At. No. Cr = 24, Mn = 25, Fe = 26, Co = 27) ","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"[Cr(CN)<sub>6</sub>]<sup>-3 </sup>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"[Mn(CN)<sub>6</sub>]<sup>-3</sup>"},{"identifier":"C","content":"[Fe(CN)<sub>6</sub>]<sup>-3</sup> "},{"identifier":"D","content":"[Co(CN)<sub>6</sub>]<sup>-3</sup>"}],"correct_options":["D"],"explanation":"<table class=\"tg\">\n  <tbody><tr>\n    <th class=\"tg-4kyz\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-4kyz\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-4kyz\"></th>\n    <th class=\"tg-bzci\">No. of unpaired electron</th>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-4kyz\">a)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-4kyz\">Co<sup>3+</sup></td>\n    <td class=\"tg-4kyz\"></td>\n    <td class=\"tg-bzci\">0</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-4kyz\">b)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-4kyz\">Fe<sup>3+</sup></td>\n    <td class=\"tg-4kyz\"></td>\n    <td class=\"tg-bzci\">1</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-4kyz\">c)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-4kyz\">Mn<sup>3+</sup></td>\n    <td class=\"tg-4kyz\"></td>\n    <td class=\"tg-bzci\">2</td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n    <td class=\"tg-4kyz\">d)</td>\n    <td class=\"tg-4kyz\">Cr<sup>3+</sup></td>\n    <td class=\"tg-4kyz\"></td>\n    <td class=\"tg-bzci\">3</td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody></table> \n<br><br>The effective magnetic moment is given by the number of unpaired electrons in a substance, the lesser the number of unpaired electrons lower is its magnetic moment in Bohr <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> Magneton and lower shall be its paramagnetism"}]}